Since $\tan{B}=\frac{7}{1}$, we have $\dfrac{AB}{AC} = \dfrac{7}{1}$, thus $$AB = 7 \cdot AC = 7 \cdot 1 = 7.$$
Then, from the Pythagorean Theorem, we have:
\begin{align*}
BC&=\sqrt{AB^2+AC^2}\\
&=\sqrt{7^2+1^2}=\sqrt{50}=\boxed{5\sqrt{2}}.
\end{align*}

