In the diagram below, \(AB = AC = 130\), \(AD = 50\), and \(CF = 90\). Compute \(\frac{[CEF]}{[DBE]}\).

[asy]
unitsize(0.025 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F;

B = (0,0);
C = (90,0);
A = intersectionpoint(arc(B,130,0,180),arc(C,130,0,180));
D = interp(A,B,50/130);
F = interp(A,C,(130+90)/130);
E = extension(B,C,D,F);

draw(C--B--A--F--D);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, W);
label("$E$", E, SW);
label("$F$", F, SE);
[/asy]

